# JavaScript

- Use modern browser-supported JavaScript. `script.js` and `admin/**/*.js` are browser code. Files in `/api` and `/lib` are Node.js CommonJS.
- Prefer `const`. Use `let` only when reassigning. Do not use `var`.
- Use `===` and `!==`. Use descriptive names and keep functions small.
- Avoid new globals. Do not use `eval` or the `Function` constructor.
- Do not use inline event handlers. Do not add a second `DOMContentLoaded` listener.
- Treat remote data as untrusted. Allow only `http:` and `https:` before setting `href` or `src`.
- Display external text with `textContent`. Never put unsanitized feed or API content in `innerHTML`.
- Handle async failures explicitly. Use `AbortController` or a timeout for external requests.
- Preserve current site behavior when adding a feature.
- Remove debug logging before production. Keep useful `console.error` logging. Do not swallow errors.
- Do not add a dependency when the browser or the platform already provides the behavior.

```javascript
const href = sanitizeOrNormalizeUrl(post.link);
if (!href) {
  return null;
}
link.href = href;
title.textContent = post.title;
```
